# neutron-owned-subsurface-reconf-keepz (revised 11-06, keepz2: + crop-origin resync)
#
# Touches: dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c, dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h.
# Two behaviors, two kill switches: NEUTRON_OWNED_RECONF_KEEPZ (z-order, unchanged from affinity2) and
# NEUTRON_CROP_ORIGIN_RESYNC (positions, new). Replaces affinity2/owned-subsurface-reconf-keepz.mypatch in the batch order.
#
# PART 1 -- OWNED-WINDOW Z-ORDER (affinity2, unchanged code)
# WHAT HAPPENED (lab, 11-05, Affinity 3.3.3; not reported by a user yet): Welcome panel > "Sign In..." opens a modal
# "Log in or sign up" dialog (WPF, owned by the main window). It was placed right but drawn BEHIND the Welcome panel
# (another owned window of the same main window), and the whole app was blocked by the invisible modal. Win32 z-order had
# the dialog on top, and so did the stacker's own log line (NT-EV restack ... order-bottom-to-top: main, welcome, dialog).
# MECHANISM: wayland_surface_reconfigure_subsurface() ran wl_subsurface_place_above(toplevel or its client surface) on
# every move/resize of an owned subsurface. That drops it to just above its parent, beneath every sibling owned window,
# and the stacker (neutron_restack_apply) then saw an unchanged Win32 order in its order cache and never repaired it.
# Fix: with the owned z-order mirror on (NEUTRON_OWNED_ZORDER), reconfigure sets the position only and leaves ordering
# to the stacker. A new wl_subsurface starts on top and the stacker orders it on show, as before.
# WINDOWS: a newly shown/activated owned window is above its owner's other owned windows (it is on top in Win32 here).
# Kill switch NEUTRON_OWNED_RECONF_KEEPZ=0.
#
# PART 2 -- CROP-ORIGIN RESYNC (new)
# WHAT HAPPENED (lab regression pass of 183rc, 11-05): "after restoring a maximized Photoshop 2026 window by
# double-clicking its caption, 183rc draws the canvas about 3 logical px off diagonally ((+6,+6) device px, 39,005 px
# changed) and keeps it there until the next input".
# NOT CAUSED BY PART 1: for Photoshop part 1 changes no Wayland request at all (its main window has no client surface of
# its own and NEUTRON_SUBSURFACE_NO_DEMOTE is on, so the old branch did nothing either), and 182 -- which has no part 1 --
# shows the same offset today. It is a race that both builds lose some of the time.
# MECHANISM: a maximized window whose frame hangs off its monitor is shown cropped (frame-spill crop): surface-local
# (0,0) is window (content_x, content_y) = (5,4) device px on the lab desk. Every subsurface of the window -- the client
# (GPU) surfaces of its child windows (Photoshop's canvas) and its owned windows (the Type Bar) -- is positioned against
# that origin. The origin changes only in wayland_surface_attach_shm, when the first buffer of the new state is attached.
# Win32 moves the children BEFORE that (logged: the canvas re-placed 9 times with the old origin 5,4 in the 170 ms before
# the restored buffer was attached), so they keep the old origin's position -- 3 logical px up and left -- until
# something places them again. If Photoshop presents the canvas once more after the attach (kd1: 5 ms after) it lands
# right; if not, it stays off until the next input.
# FIX: neutron_resync_crop_origin(), called at the end of attach_shm when the crop origin changed (both callers hold
# win_data_mutex and commit the surface right after): re-place every client subsurface on this wl_surface (from the client
# rect / ancestor clip it was last placed from, now remembered in wayland_client_surface) and every owned subsurface
# (wayland_surface_reconfigure_subsurface's arithmetic, factored out as neutron_subsurface_position) with the NEW origin.
# A wl_subsurface position is parent state, so it lands in the same commit as the new crop. A client whose viewport
# changes too (its edges round differently against the new origin: Photoshop's canvas 1521x971 -> 1521x972 logical) is
# committed in sync mode and the parent committed there, as wayland_client_surface_attach_rect does, so its size lands in
# the same frame instead of at its next present (a first build without this left the canvas 1 px short until then).
# No place_above/below: the order stays the stacker's. One ERR line per origin change ("neutron-crop-resync: ...").
# WINDOWS: a restored (or maximized) window's contents -- child windows and owned windows -- land at the new position in
# the same frame as the window; nothing waits for the next input.
# NOT COVERED: xdg popups (menus) open while the origin changes keep their position until they are re-shown;
# a client surface that never went through reconfigure_client (no stored rect) is skipped.
#
# LAB EVIDENCE
# Lab desk u (2 outputs: 175% + 200%), host NVIDIA 615.78 / Mesa 26.2.6 / kernel 7.3.1 (re-measured today), PgD-ps2 reflinks
# provisioned on each arm's runtime. Ps sequence: open doc, type text, Esc, caption double-click = restore. Judge: canvas
# position at the restore (offset.py; stale = 6,5 capture px = 3 logical up-left) and in-run Ctrl+H x2 (forces a canvas
# present: a stale canvas jumps +6,+5 to the correct place; a correct one does not move).
#   182 (no part 1 at all):                stale 2/2   (judge confirmed on the 2nd: Ctrl+H moved it to == the correct frame)
#   183rc:                                 stale 1/2
#   183rc NEUTRON_OWNED_RECONF_KEEPZ=0:    stale 0/2   (last night 182 0/1, kill 0/1, 183rc 2/2 = the same race)
#   183rc + diag log (kd1):                correct; log: canvas placed 9x with origin 5,4 before the restored attach,
#                                          re-placed with 0,0 by a present 5 ms after it
#   11.10-183k2 (this patch):              offset 0/2 (g1, g2: max1 and max1+8 s full frames == the correct frame, 0 px;
#                                          log "crop origin 5,4 -> 0,0: re-placed 1 client (1 resized) and 1 owned")
#   11.10-183k2 NEUTRON_CROP_ORIGIN_RESYNC=0: stale 1/3 (h3 stale, judge moved it +6,+5; h2, h4 correct; h1 void: Ps GPU
#                                          check dialog at start, no document)
#   First build of part 2 (position only): position right 1/1 but the canvas 1 logical px short until the next present ->
#                                          the sync-commit for a resized client (this version).
# Affinity sign-in dialog (fake xdg-open logs the "Log in or sign up" click only if it reaches the dialog), 11.10-183k2:
#   on: dialog on top, hand-off 2/2 (screenshot: dialog over the Welcome panel); NEUTRON_OWNED_RECONF_KEEPZ=0: hidden 2/2.
# 11.10-183k2 vs 182, n=1: Premiere 2026 open project, seek, text, maximize: every frame 0 px (resync re-placed the Program
#   Monitor client at the maximize; the restore double-click missed on both arms, no owned windows in that sequence).
#   Photoshop Color panel dragged out to float: 0 px vs 182; moving it +200,+120: rect moved exactly, drawn at the new place,
#   nothing left behind (183k2; the 182 rerun opened no document = void).
# Kill switches: NEUTRON_OWNED_RECONF_KEEPZ=0 (part 1), NEUTRON_CROP_ORIGIN_RESYNC=0 (part 2).

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
@@ -373,6 +373,11 @@
     /* NEUTRON: the window is entirely outside its ancestors' client areas (scrolled out of view), so it is
      * shrunk to 1x1 inside the toplevel and placed below it -- kept MAPPED for the reason above. */
     BOOL clipped_out;
+    /* NEUTRON crop-origin resync: the client rect and ancestor clip (toplevel client coordinates, which do not depend
+     * on the toplevel's frame-spill crop) this surface was last placed from, so it can be placed again when only the
+     * crop origin changes. */
+    RECT neutron_rect, neutron_clip;
+    BOOL neutron_rect_set, neutron_clip_set;
     /* NEUTRON: the viewport state last sent (to send only changes), and whether it changed since the surface was
      * last committed -- viewport state is double-buffered on the CLIENT surface, so without a commit it waits
      * for the app's next present (forever, for a paused video). */
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -1258,12 +1258,15 @@
     return on;
 }
 
+static void neutron_resync_crop_origin(struct wayland_surface *surface, int old_x, int old_y);
+
